package raw

// SkillWeaponTypes mirrors the `weaponTypes` tables of PoB's hand-written skill data
// (src/Data/Skills/*.lua), keyed by granted-effect id. Values are PoB's OWN weapon-type names
// -- src/Modules/Data.lua:205-221's `weaponTypeInfo` keys, which data.ItemClassName transcribes
// verbatim -- NOT go-pob-data's plural ItemClasses.
//
// CalcActiveSkill.lua:229-254 collects the active gem's table plus every support gem's, then
// getWeaponFlags (:143-174) rejects a weapon absent from ANY of them by returning a nil flag set
// beside a non-nil info. That pair is what :250 tests to disable the skill; without the table
// the pair can never occur and the arm is unreachable.
//
// ABSENT means "no restriction" and is NOT the same as an empty list: Lua's `{ ge.weaponTypes }`
// collapses a nil to a zero-length list so :149's ipairs never runs, whereas a present-but-empty
// table would iterate once and reject every weapon. Reading a missing key out of this map yields
// a nil slice, and calculator.getWeaponFlags skips empty lists for exactly that reason.
//
// GENERATED by `gopob skill-weapon-types-emit` from scripts/gamedatadump skill-weapon-types: a support's
// GrantedEffects.WeaponRestrictions, an active skill's ActiveSkills.WeaponRestrictions, mapped as PoB's
// Export/Scripts/skills.lua maps them. Regenerate with `task data-regen -- --only skill-weapon-types`.
// 2 of 3 skills declare weaponTypes -- 1 active, 1 support.
var SkillWeaponTypes = map[string][]string{
	"SupportThing": {"Claw", "Dagger"},
	// src/Data/Skills/act_dex.lua:77
	"ToxicRain": {"Bow"},
}
